>> title: Gyoza
>> category: Dumplings & Rolls
>> tags: pork, japanese, dumpling, pan-fry, cabbage
>> counters: Ramen Shop, Japanese Home Cooking
>> aka: gyoza, gyōza, 餃子, pot stickers, potstickers, yaki gyoza, yaki-gyoza, fried dumplings, pork dumplings, an order of six
>> pairs-with: shoyu-ramen, tonkotsu-ramen
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hr 45 min
>> slack: narrow — the cabbage is wrung until almost nothing more comes; a wet filling steams grey inside a wrapper that then splits open

>> step: The filling is wrung dry and it is pleated on one side only so it sits flat in the pan.
A gyoza is not a jiaozi: the wrapper is thinner, the filling is wrung dry, and it is pleated on one side only so it sits flat in the pan.

>> step: knead 8 min to a firm dough
Knead @all-purpose flour{2%cups}(260 g), @fine sea salt{1/2%tsp}(3 g) and @boiling water{2/3%cup}(160 mL) together ~knead{8%min}, until it is firm and smooth and springs back slowly.

>> step: rest 30 min under a bowl
Rest @&(~1)dough{} under an upturned bowl ~rest{30%min}.

>> step: salt 20 min, then wring dry
Salt @napa cabbage{3%cups}(225 g; chopped fine) with @kosher salt{1%tsp}(5 g) and ~drain{20%min}, then take it up in a cloth and wring it out until almost nothing more comes.

>> step: beat one way 3 min until sticky
Beat @ground pork{8%oz}(225 g), @garlic chives{1/2%cup}(30 g; chopped), @garlic{2%cloves}(grated), @fresh ginger{1%Tbs}(grated), @soy sauce{1%Tbs}(15 mL), @toasted sesame oil{2%tsp}(10 mL), @sake{1%Tbs}(15 mL), @granulated sugar{1%tsp}(4 g) and @white pepper{1/4%tsp} into @&(~1)wrung cabbage{} ~beat{3%min}, stirring in one direction only until the mass turns tacky and holds a fingerprint.

>> step: roll thin, cut 3.5-in rounds
Roll @&(~3)rested dough{} out thin on @cornstarch{2%Tbs}(20 g) and cut it into 3 1/2-inch rounds, working each round thinner at the edge than the middle.

>> step: fill, pleat one side, press flat
Fill @&(~1)wrappers{} with a scant tablespoon of @&(~2)filling{} each, wet the rim, and pleat the near side only — six or seven folds facing one way — then press the base flat.

>> step: fry 3 min, steam 6 min, crisp 2 min
Fry @&(~1)gyoza{} flat-side-down in @neutral oil{1%Tbs}(15 mL) in a lidded #skillet{} ~fry{3%min} until the bases are gold, pour in @water{1/3%cup}(80 mL), cover and ~steam{6%min}, then uncover and ~fry{2%min} until the base crackles.
